/-!
# The semi-free resolution of the ground ring over the chains on the loops of a circle

Brown's twisted tensor product resolves the ground ring `R` over the chains `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` on the
Moore loops of a CW complex `B` by a semi-free module with one free generator for each cell,
attached along a cycle representing the attaching map of the cell. For the circle, with one
`0`-cell `e₀` at the base point and one `1`-cell `e₁` attached along a loop `γ` going once around,
this module is

`K = C_*(Ω_b B; R) e₀ ⊕ C_*(Ω_b B; R) e₁`,  `D e₀ = 0`,  `D e₁ = ([γ] - [1]) e₀`,

where `[γ]` is the point chain of the Moore loop `γ` and `[1]` the unit. As a row-finite twisting
cocycle on the generators `Unit ⊕ Unit`, with `e₀ = Sum.inl ()` of index `0` and
`e₁ = Sum.inr ()` of index `1`, this is `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ`: the generator `e₁` is
attached (`TauCeti.RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.attach`) along the cycle `([γ] - [1]) e₀` to the free
module on `e₀` with zero differential (`TauCeti.loopCellCocycle_m_inr`). It is one-sided, so the
module is semi-free (`TauCeti.loopCellCocycle_m_eq_zero_of_le`). The differential of a vector
`α e₀ + β e₁` is `dα ± β ([γ] - [1])` on `e₀` and `dβ` on `e₁`
(`TauCeti.loopCellCocycle_differential_apply`). The cocycle is defined for every Moore loop of
every space.

The augmentation `ε : K → R` takes the augmentation of the coefficient of `e₀`
(`TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation`). It is linear over the augmentation of the loop chain algebra
(`TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation_smul`), vanishes on boundaries
(`TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation_differential`) and takes the value `1` on the cycle `e₀`.

The main result is that `ε` is a quasi-isomorphism onto `R` when `B` is aspherical with fundamental
group infinite cyclic generated by the class of `γ`, as for the circle: every cycle of `K` with
augmentation zero is a boundary
(`TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`). Over an
aspherical space the homology of `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` is the group ring `R[π₁(B, b)]`, concentrated in
degree zero, so the homology of `K` is that of the complex `R[π₁] → R[π₁]` given by right
multiplication by `g - 1`, where `g` is the class of `γ`. That map is injective since `g` has
infinite order, and its cokernel is `R` through the augmentation since `g` generates. The proof
runs this argument on representatives, using that a cycle of the loop chain algebra whose
degree-zero truncation vanishes is a boundary
(`TauCeti.exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero`).

The loop `γ` in the attaching row cannot be dropped. With the zero cocycle on the same two
generators, `e₁` is a cycle of augmentation zero which is not a boundary, for every space and every
nontrivial ring `R` (`TauCeti.exists_notMem_range_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero`): that module
is the direct sum of two shifted copies of `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`, whose homology is not that of a
point.

In Brown's theory the resolution is compared with the chains `C_*(P_b B; R)` on the based path
space `P_b B` of Moore paths from `b`, a left module over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` through concatenation in
front (`TauCeti.pathFromChain_isDGLeftModule`). The comparison `f : K → C_*(P_b B; R)`
(`TauCeti.loopCellComparison`) is linear over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` and sends `e₀` to the point chain of
the constant path of length zero at `b`, and `e₁` to the `1`-cube of truncations of `γ`, which
runs from `γ`, read as a path from `b`, to the constant path: minus the cone on the point chain of
`γ` along the contraction of the based path space by truncation. The boundary of that cube is the
image of the attaching cycle `([γ] - [1]) e₀`, so `f` is a chain map
(`TauCeti.linearCombination_loopCellComparison_differential`), and it preserves the
augmentations. This holds for every Moore loop of every space. Since the based path space is
contractible, `f` is a quasi-isomorphism exactly when `ε` is
(`TauCeti.forall_exists_loopCellComparison_iff_forall_exists_loopCellCocycle`), in particular for
the circle.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ`: the twisting cocycle of one `1`-cell attached along `γ` to one
  `0`-cell.
* `TauCeti.loopCellAugmentation B b R`: the augmentation of its free module.
* `TauCeti.loopCellComparison H R γ`: the images of the generators under the comparison with the
  chains on the based path space.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle_differential_apply`: the differential on `α e₀ + β e₁`.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`: over an
  aspherical space whose fundamental group is infinite cyclic, generated by the class of `γ`, the
  augmentation is a quasi-isomorphism.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`: the
  case of the circle and its counterclockwise loop.
* `TauCeti.exists_notMem_range_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero`: the zero cocycle on the same
  generators does not resolve `R`.
* `TauCeti.linearCombination_loopCellComparison_differential`,
  `TauCeti.cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_linearCombination_loopCellComparison`: the comparison is
  a chain map preserving the augmentations.
* `TauCeti.forall_exists_loopCellComparison_iff_forall_exists_loopCellCocycle`: the comparison is
  a quasi-isomorphism exactly when the augmentation of the free module is.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellComparison_eq`: under the
  hypotheses of the resolution theorem, the comparison is a quasi-isomorphism.
* `TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_of_loopCellComparison_eq`: the case of
  the circle and its counterclockwise loop.

## References

* E. H. Brown, *Twisted tensor products, I*, Ann. of Math. (2) 69 (1959), 223–246.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Floer homology with DG coefficients.
  Applications to cotangent bundles*, arXiv:2404.07953, §1.4.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Morse homology with differential graded
  coefficients*, Progress in Mathematics 360, Birkhäuser, 2025, Chapters 3--4.
-/

public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicTopology

open scoped Topology

universe u

namespace TauCeti

section Cocycle

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} (R : Type*) [CommRing R]

/-- **The twisting cocycle of one `1`-cell attached along a loop.** On the generators
`Unit ⊕ Unit`, the `0`-cell `e₀ = Sum.inl ()` of index `0` has zero row, and the `1`-cell
`e₁ = Sum.inr ()` of index `1` is attached (`TauCeti.RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.attach`) along the
cycle `([γ] - [1]) e₀`: the difference of the point chain of the Moore loop `γ` and the unit of
`C_*(Ω_b B; R)`. For a circle and a loop going once around, this is Brown's semi-free resolution
of `R` over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`. -/
def loopCellCocycle (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    RowFiniteTwistingCocycle (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (Unit ⊕ Unit) (Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ 0) (fun _ ↦ 1)) :=
  (0 : RowFiniteTwistingCocycle (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      Unit (fun _ ↦ 0)).attach
    (fun _ ↦ Finsupp.single () (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
      (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1))
    (fun _ _ ↦ by
      have hp : cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
          (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) ∈
            cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 := by
        simpa using cubicalChainLof_mem (MooreLoopSpace B b) R
          (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ))
      simpa using sub_mem hp (SetLike.one_mem_graded (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)))
    (fun _ ↦ by
      rw [RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.zero_m, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero,
        Finsupp.mapRange.linearMap_apply, Finsupp.mapRange_single, map_sub,
        cubicalChainDifferential_lof_zero, (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).map_one_eq_zero, sub_zero,
        Finsupp.single_zero])

variable {R}

@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_m_inl (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (loopCellCocycle R γ).m (Sum.inl ()) = 0 := by
  simp [loopCellCocycle]

/-- The row of `e₁` is `([γ] - [1]) e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_m_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (loopCellCocycle R γ).m (Sum.inr ()) = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ())
      (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
        (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1) := by
  rw [loopCellCocycle, RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.attach_m_inr, Finsupp.mapDomain_single]

/-- The cocycle is one-sided, so its free module is semi-free
(`TauCeti.RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.wellFounded_mem_support`). -/
theorem loopCellCocycle_m_eq_zero_of_le (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) {x y : Unit ⊕ Unit}
    (h : Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ (0 : ℤ)) (fun _ ↦ 1) x ≤ Sum.elim (fun _ ↦ (0 : ℤ)) (fun _ ↦ 1) y) :
    (loopCellCocycle R γ).m x y = 0 :=
  RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.attach_m_eq_zero_of_le _ _ _ (fun _ _ _ ↦ by simp)
    (fun _ _ h ↦ absurd h (by simp)) x y h

/-- The differential of the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` on `α e₀ + β e₁`: the
coefficient of `e₀` is `dα + κ(β) ([γ] - [1])`, with `κ` the Koszul sign twist, and the coefficient
of `e₁` is `dβ`. -/
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_apply (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ())
          (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inl ())) +
          (InternalGrading.ofDecomposition (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist
              1 (u (Sum.inr ())) *
            (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
              (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1)) +
        Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ())
          (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inr ()))) := by
  have hu : u = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (u (Sum.inl ())) +
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (u (Sum.inr ())) := by
    ext i
    rcases i with ⟨⟩ | ⟨⟩ <;> simp
  conv_lhs => rw [hu]
  rw [map_add, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_single_koszulTwist,
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_single_koszulTwist, loopCellCocycle_m_inl, loopCellCocycle_m_inr,
    smul_zero, add_zero, Finsupp.smul_single, smul_eq_mul, Finsupp.single_add]
  abel

/-- The coefficient of `e₀` in the differential of `u` is `d(u e₀) + κ(u e₁) ([γ] - [1])`, with
`κ` the Koszul sign twist. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_apply_inl (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u
          (Sum.inl ()) =
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inl ())) +
        (InternalGrading.ofDecomposition (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist
            1 (u (Sum.inr ())) *
          (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
            (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1) := by
  simp [loopCellCocycle_differential_apply]

/-- The coefficient of `e₁` in the differential of `u` is `d(u e₁)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_apply_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u
          (Sum.inr ()) =
      cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R (u (Sum.inr ())) := by
  simp [loopCellCocycle_differential_apply]

/-- The differential of `α e₀` is `(dα) e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inl (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (α : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) α) =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R α) := by
  simp [loopCellCocycle_differential_apply]

/-- The differential of `β e₁` is `κ(β) ([γ] - [1]) e₀ + (dβ) e₁`, with `κ` the Koszul sign
twist. -/
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (β : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) β) =
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ())
          ((InternalGrading.ofDecomposition
              (cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)).koszulTwist 1 β *
            (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
              (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1)) +
        Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) (cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R β) := by
  simp [loopCellCocycle_differential_apply]

variable (B b R) in
/-- The augmentation of the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ`: the augmentation of the
coefficient of the generator `e₀ = Sum.inl ()` of index zero. -/
def loopCellAugmentation : (Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) →ₗ[R] R :=
  (loopChainAugmentation B b R).toAlgHom.toLinearMap ∘ₗ Finsupp.lapply (Sum.inl ())

theorem loopCellAugmentation_apply (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R u = loopChainAugmentation B b R (u (Sum.inl ())) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The augmentation is linear over the augmentation of the loop chain algebra. -/
theorem loopCellAugmentation_smul (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R (a • u) =
      loopChainAugmentation B b R a * loopCellAugmentation B b R u := by
  simp [loopCellAugmentation_apply]

/-- The augmentation takes the augmentation of a coefficient of `e₀`; in particular it takes the
value `1` on the cycle `e₀`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellAugmentation_single_inl (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) a) = loopChainAugmentation B b R a := by
  simp [loopCellAugmentation_apply]

/-- The augmentation vanishes on the multiples of `e₁`. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellAugmentation_single_inr (a : loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) a) = 0 := by
  simp [loopCellAugmentation_apply]

variable (B b R) in
/-- The augmentation is surjective: it takes `r e₀` to `r`. -/
theorem loopCellAugmentation_surjective : Function.Surjective (loopCellAugmentation B b R) :=
  fun r ↦ ⟨Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R _ r), by simp⟩

/-- The generator `e₀` is a cycle. -/
theorem loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inl_one (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m
        (Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) 1) = 0 := by
  rw [RowFiniteTwistingCocycle.differential_single_one _ (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R),
    loopCellCocycle_m_inl]

/-- The augmentation vanishes on boundaries. -/
@[simp]
theorem loopCellAugmentation_differential (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    loopCellAugmentation B b R
        (rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u) =
      0 := by
  simp [loopCellAugmentation_apply]

variable (B b R) in
/-- **The loop in the attaching row cannot be dropped.** For every space and every nontrivial
ring `R`, the free module of the zero cocycle on the generators `Unit ⊕ Unit` has a cycle of
augmentation zero which is not a boundary, namely `e₁ = Sum.inr ()`. So its augmentation is not
a quasi-isomorphism onto `R`, unlike that of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` over a circle. -/
theorem exists_notMem_range_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero [Nontrivial R] :
    ∃ u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R,
      rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
          (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) 0 u = 0 ∧
        loopCellAugmentation B b R u = 0 ∧
        u ∉ LinearMap.range (rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
          (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) 0) := by
  refine ⟨Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) 1, ?_, loopCellAugmentation_single_inr 1, ?_⟩
  · simp [(loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).map_one_eq_zero]
  · rintro ⟨v, hv⟩
    -- The coefficient of `e₁` would be a boundary with augmentation `1`.
    have h := congrArg (fun w ↦ loopChainAugmentation B b R (w (Sum.inr ()))) hv
    simp only [rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_zero, Finsupp.mapRange.linearMap_apply,
      Finsupp.mapRange_apply, DGAlgAugmentation.map_d, Finsupp.single_eq_same, map_one] at h
    exact zero_ne_one h

end Cocycle

section Comparison

variable {B : Type*} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} (H : Type*) (R : Type*) [CommRing R]

/-- **The comparison of the loop-cell module with the chains on the based path space**, on the
generators. The generator `e₀ = Sum.inl ()` goes to the point chain of the constant path of length
zero at `b`. The generator `e₁ = Sum.inr ()` goes to minus the cone, along the contraction
`TauCeti.MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy` of the based path space, on the point chain of `γ` read as
a path from `b`: the `1`-cube of the truncations of `γ`, run from `γ` to the constant path. The
comparison itself is the map `Finsupp.linearCombination` of these images, linear over
`C_*(Ω_b B; R)`. -/
def loopCellComparison (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    Unit ⊕ Unit → cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R :=
  Sum.elim
    (fun _ ↦ cubicalChainModuleLof _ H R 0
      (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point (MoorePathFrom.refl B b))))
    (fun _ ↦ -cubicalChainModuleCone R MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy
      (cubicalChainModuleLof _ H R 0
        (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point (γ • MoorePathFrom.refl B b)))))

variable {H R}

@[simp]
theorem loopCellComparison_inl (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    loopCellComparison H R γ (Sum.inl ()) = cubicalChainModuleLof _ H R 0
      (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point (MoorePathFrom.refl B b))) :=
  (rfl)

@[simp]
theorem loopCellComparison_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    loopCellComparison H R γ (Sum.inr ()) =
      -cubicalChainModuleCone R MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy
        (cubicalChainModuleLof _ H R 0
          (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point (γ • MoorePathFrom.refl B b)))) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The image of `e₁` bounds the image of its attaching cycle `([γ] - [1]) e₀`: the point chain of
`γ`, read as a path from `b`, minus that of the constant path. -/
theorem cubicalChainModuleDifferential_loopCellComparison_inr (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    cubicalChainModuleDifferential _ H R (loopCellComparison H R γ (Sum.inr ())) =
      (cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
          (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ)) - 1) •
        loopCellComparison H R γ (Sum.inl ()) := by
  have h := cubicalChainModuleDifferential_cone_add_cone_differential
    MoorePathFrom.truncateHomotopy (cubicalChainModuleLof (MoorePathFrom B b) H R 0
      (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point (γ • MoorePathFrom.refl B b))))
  simp only [cubicalChainModuleDifferential_lof_zero, map_zero, add_zero] at h
  rw [loopCellComparison_inr, map_neg, h]
  simp [sub_smul, lof_smul_cubicalChainModuleLof, NormalizedCubicalChain.augment_ofCube]

/-- **The comparison is a chain map**: it carries the differential of the free module of
`TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` to the boundary of the chains on the based path space. -/
theorem linearCombination_loopCellComparison_differential (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b)
    (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra B b R) (loopCellComparison H R γ)
        (rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
          (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u) =
      cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
        (Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra B b R) (loopCellComparison H R γ) u) := by
  refine (forall_linearCombination_rowFiniteTwistedDifferential_iff
    (pathFromChain_isDGLeftModule B b H R) _ _).2 (fun x ↦ ?_) u
  rcases x with ⟨⟨⟩⟩ | ⟨⟨⟩⟩
  · simp
  · rw [loopCellCocycle_m_inr, Finsupp.linearCombination_single,
      cubicalChainModuleDifferential_loopCellComparison_inr]

/-- **The comparison preserves the augmentations.** -/
@[simp]
theorem cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_linearCombination_loopCellComparison
    (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) :
    cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
        (Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra B b R) (loopCellComparison H R γ) u) =
      loopCellAugmentation B b R u := by
  induction u using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp
  | add u v hu hv => rw [map_add, map_add, hu, hv, map_add]
  | single x a =>
    rcases x with ⟨⟨⟩⟩ | ⟨⟨⟩⟩
    · simp [pathFromChainAugmentation_smul, NormalizedCubicalChain.augment_ofCube]
    · simp [pathFromChainAugmentation_smul]

/-- **The comparison is a quasi-isomorphism exactly when the loop-cell module resolves `R`.** Since
the based path space is contractible, its chains have the homology of a point, through the
augmentation, which the comparison `f` preserves. So the relative cycles `(u, w)` of `f`, cycles
`u` of the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` with `f u = ∂ w`, are all relative
boundaries (`u = D u'` and `w = f u' + ∂ v`, so that `f` is a quasi-isomorphism of DG left modules
over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`) exactly when every cycle of augmentation zero of the free module is a
boundary. -/
theorem forall_exists_loopCellComparison_iff_forall_exists_loopCellCocycle
    (γ : MooreLoopSpace B b) :
    (∀ (u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) (w : cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R),
      rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
          (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
          (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u = 0 →
        Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra B b R) (loopCellComparison H R γ) u =
          cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R w →
        ∃ u' v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
            (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
            (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u' = u ∧
          Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra B b R) (loopCellComparison H R γ) u' +
              cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R v = w) ↔
      ∀ u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R,
        rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
            (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
            (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u = 0 →
          loopCellAugmentation B b R u = 0 →
          ∃ v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
            (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
            (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m v =
              u := by
  set D := rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
    (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m with hD
  set f := Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra B b R) (loopCellComparison H R γ) with hf
  set ε := cubicalChainModuleAugmentation (MoorePathFrom B b) H R
  -- `f` is a chain map.
  have hfD : ∀ x, cubicalChainModuleDifferential _ H R (f x) = f (D x) := fun x ↦
    (linearCombination_loopCellComparison_differential γ x).symm
  constructor
  · -- A cycle `u` of augmentation zero maps to a cycle of augmentation zero, which bounds.
    intro hrel u hu hε
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := exists_pathFromChainDifferential_eq_of_augmentation_eq_zero (m := f u)
      (by rw [hfD, hu, map_zero])
      ((cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_linearCombination_loopCellComparison γ u).trans hε)
    obtain ⟨u', -, hu', -⟩ := hrel u w hu hw.symm
    exact ⟨u', hu'⟩
  · intro hres u w hu huw
    -- The cycle `u` has augmentation `ε (f u) = ε (∂ w) = 0`, so it is a boundary `D u₁`.
    obtain ⟨u₁, hu₁⟩ := hres u hu (by
      rw [← cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_linearCombination_loopCellComparison (H := H) γ, ← hf,
        huw, cubicalChainModuleAugmentation_differential])
    -- Then `w - f u₁` is a cycle; subtracting the image of a multiple `u₀` of the cycle `e₀`
    -- leaves a cycle of augmentation zero, which bounds since the based path space is
    -- contractible.
    set u₀ : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R :=
      Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (algebraMap R _ (ε (w - f u₁)))
    have hDu₀ : D u₀ = 0 := by
      rw [hD, loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inl,
        (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R).map_algebraMap, Finsupp.single_zero]
    obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := exists_pathFromChainDifferential_eq_of_augmentation_eq_zero
      (m := w - f u₁ - f u₀)
      (by simp only [map_sub, hfD, hu₁, hDu₀, huw, map_zero, sub_self])
      (by simp [hf, u₀, ε])
    exact ⟨u₁ + u₀, v, by rw [map_add, hu₁, hDu₀, add_zero], by rw [hv, map_add]; abel⟩

end Comparison

section Resolution

variable {B : Type u} [TopologicalSpace B] {b : B} {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-- **Brown's resolution of the ground ring over the chains on the loops of a circle.** Let `B` be
aspherical at `b`, and let the class `g` of the Moore loop `γ` generate the fundamental group
`π₁(B, b)` and have infinite order, as for a loop going once around a circle. Then every cycle of
the free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` whose augmentation vanishes is a boundary. Since
the augmentation vanishes on boundaries and takes the value `1` on the cycle `e₀`, it is a
quasi-isomorphism onto `R`: the module is a semi-free resolution of `R` over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)`. -/
theorem exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero
    (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) B b)) {γ : MooreLoopSpace B b}
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ) = ⊤)
    (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ))
    {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u = 0)
    (hε : loopCellAugmentation B b R u = 0) :
    ∃ v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m v = u := by
  set D := rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
    (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
    (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m with hD
  set d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R
  set T := loopChainToGroupAlgebra B b R
  set g := MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ
  set p := cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0
    (NormalizedCubicalChain.ofCube _ R (SingularCube.point γ))
  have hDsq (w) : D (D w) = 0 :=
    (loopCellCocycle R γ).differential_sq_zero (loopChain_isDGAlgebra B b R) w
  have hTp : T (p - 1) = MonoidAlgebra.single g 1 - 1 := by
    rw [map_sub, map_one, loopChainToGroupAlgebra_lof_zero, loopZeroChainToGroupAlgebra_ofCube,
      SingularCube.point_apply]
  -- A cycle `α e₀` whose coefficient has vanishing truncation is a boundary.
  have hbound (w : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R) (hw1 : w (Sum.inr ()) = 0)
      (hDw : D w = 0) (hT : T (w (Sum.inl ())) = 0) : ∃ v, D v = w := by
    have hw : w = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (w (Sum.inl ())) := by
      ext i
      rcases i with ⟨⟩ | ⟨⟩ <;> simp [hw1]
    have hdw : d (w (Sum.inl ())) = 0 := by
      have := congrArg (· (Sum.inl ())) hDw
      rw [hw, hD, loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inl] at this
      simpa using this
    obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ := exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero R hB
      hdw hT
    exact ⟨Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) α,
      by rw [hD, loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inl, hα, ← hw]⟩
  have hu0 := congrArg (· (Sum.inl ())) hu
  have hu1 := congrArg (· (Sum.inr ())) hu
  simp only [hD, loopCellCocycle_differential_apply_inl, loopCellCocycle_differential_apply_inr,
    Finsupp.coe_zero, Pi.zero_apply] at hu0 hu1
  -- The coefficient of `e₁` is a cycle whose truncation `t` satisfies `t (g - 1) = 0`, so `t = 0`.
  have hTu1 : T (u (Sum.inr ())) = 0 := by
    have h := congrArg T hu0
    rw [map_add, loopChainToGroupAlgebra_differential, zero_add, map_mul, hTp,
      loopChainToGroupAlgebra_koszulTwist, map_zero,
      ← zero_mul (MonoidAlgebra.single g 1 - 1)] at h
    exact (isRegular_single_sub_one_of_not_isOfFinOrder hinf).right h
  obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := exists_cubicalChainDifferential_eq_of_loopChainToGroupAlgebra_eq_zero R hB
    hu1 hTu1
  -- Subtracting the boundary of `β e₁` leaves a cycle `w` supported on `e₀`, of augmentation zero.
  set w := u - D (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) β) with hw
  have hw1 : w (Sum.inr ()) = 0 := by simp [hw, hD, loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inr, hβ]
  have hDw : D w = 0 := by rw [hw, map_sub, hu, hDsq, sub_zero]
  have hεw : loopChainAugmentation B b R (w (Sum.inl ())) = 0 := by
    rw [← loopCellAugmentation_apply, hw, map_sub, hε, hD, loopCellAugmentation_differential,
      sub_zero]
  -- The truncation of `w e₀` has augmentation zero, so it is a left multiple of `g - 1`.
  have hker :
      T (w (Sum.inl ())) ∈ RingHom.ker (MonoidAlgebra.augmentation R (FundamentalGroup B b)) := by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, augmentation_loopChainToGroupAlgebra, hεw]
  rw [MonoidAlgebra.ker_augmentation_eq_span_of_closure_eq_top R
    (s := {g}) (by rw [← Subgroup.zpowers_eq_closure, hgen]), Set.image_singleton,
    Ideal.mem_span_singleton'] at hker
  obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ := hker
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := loopZeroChainToGroupAlgebra_surjective (R := R) (x := b) h
  -- Subtracting the boundary of `δ e₁`, for a zero chain `δ` lifting the multiplier, leaves a
  -- cycle supported on `e₀` with vanishing truncation.
  set δ := cubicalChainLof (MooreLoopSpace B b) R 0 c
  have hDδ : D (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) δ) = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl ()) (δ * (p - 1)) := by
    rw [hD, loopCellCocycle_differential_single_inr,
      koszulTwist_one_eq_negOnePow_smul (R := R)
        (by simpa using cubicalChainLof_mem (MooreLoopSpace B b) R c),
      Int.negOnePow_zero, one_smul, cubicalChainDifferential_lof_zero, Finsupp.single_zero,
      add_zero]
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := hbound (w - D (Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) δ)) (by simp [hw1, hDδ])
    (by rw [map_sub, hDw, hDsq, sub_zero])
    (by rw [hDδ, Finsupp.sub_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same, map_sub, map_mul,
      loopChainToGroupAlgebra_lof_zero, hc, hTp, hh, sub_self])
  refine ⟨v + Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) δ + Finsupp.single (Sum.inr ()) β, ?_⟩
  rw [map_add, map_add, hv, hw]
  abel

/-- **The loop-cell comparison is a quasi-isomorphism for aspherical spaces with infinite cyclic
fundamental group.** Under the hypotheses of
`TauCeti.exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero`, every relative
cycle `(u, w)` of the comparison `f = TauCeti.loopCellComparison`, a cycle `u` of the free module
of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R γ` with `f u = ∂ w`, is a relative boundary: `u = D u'` and
`w = f u' + ∂ v`. So `f` is a quasi-isomorphism of DG left modules over `C_*(Ω_b B; R)` onto the
chains `C_*(P_b B; R)` on the based path space. -/
theorem exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellComparison_eq
    {H : Type*} (hB : ∀ n : ℕ, Subsingleton (π_ (n + 2) B b)) {γ : MooreLoopSpace B b}
    (hgen : Subgroup.zpowers (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ) = ⊤)
    (hinf : ¬IsOfFinOrder (MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom b γ))
    {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra B b R} {w : cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom B b) H R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u = 0)
    (huw : Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra B b R) (loopCellComparison H R γ) u =
      cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R w) :
    ∃ u' v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra B b R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace B b) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace B b) R) (loopCellCocycle R γ).m u' = u ∧
      Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra B b R) (loopCellComparison H R γ) u' +
          cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom B b) H R v = w :=
  (forall_exists_loopCellComparison_iff_forall_exists_loopCellCocycle γ).2
    (fun _ hu hε ↦ exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero hB hgen
      hinf hu hε) u w hu huw

end Resolution
section Circle

/-- **Brown's resolution for the circle.** For the complex unit circle, based at `1`, with its
`1`-cell attached along the counterclockwise loop `t ↦ exp(2πit)`, every cycle of the free module
of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R` whose augmentation vanishes is a boundary: the module is a
semi-free resolution of `R` over the chains `C_*(Ω_1 S¹; R)` on the Moore loops of the circle. -/
theorem exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero
    {R : Type} [CommRing R] {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (loopCellCocycle R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop).m u = 0)
    (hε : loopCellAugmentation Circle 1 R u = 0) :
    ∃ v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (loopCellCocycle R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop).m v = u := by
  -- `MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom` takes the inverse of the path class of the loop.
  have hg : MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom (1 : Circle) Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop =
      (FundamentalGroup.fromPath (Path.Homotopic.Quotient.mk Circle.expLoop))⁻¹ := by
    rw [MooreLoopSpace.fundamentalGroupHom_apply, Path.toPath_toMooreLoop]
  refine exists_loopCellCocycle_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero
    (fun n ↦ inferInstance) ?_ ?_ hu hε
  · rw [hg, Subgroup.zpowers_inv, Circle.zpowers_fromPath_expLoop]
  · rw [hg, isOfFinOrder_inv_iff]
    exact Circle.not_isOfFinOrder_fromPath_expLoop

/-- **Brown's resolution of the circle is quasi-isomorphic to the chains on its based path space.**
For the complex unit circle, based at `1`, with its `1`-cell attached along the counterclockwise
loop `t ↦ exp(2πit)`, every relative cycle of the comparison `TauCeti.loopCellComparison` from the
free module of `TauCeti.loopCellCocycle R` to the chains on the Moore paths from `1` is a relative
boundary: the comparison is a quasi-isomorphism of DG left modules over `C_*(Ω_1 S¹; R)`. -/
theorem exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_of_loopCellComparison_eq
    {H : Type*} {R : Type} [CommRing R] {u : Unit ⊕ Unit →₀ loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R}
    {w : cubicalChainModule (MoorePathFrom Circle 1) H R}
    (hu : rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
      (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
      (loopCellCocycle R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop).m u = 0)
    (huw : Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
      (loopCellComparison H R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop) u =
        cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom Circle 1) H R w) :
    ∃ u' v, rowFiniteTwistedDifferential (R := R) (A := loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
        (𝒜 := cubicalChainGrading (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
        (d := cubicalChainDifferential (MooreLoopSpace Circle 1) R)
        (loopCellCocycle R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop).m u' = u ∧
      Finsupp.linearCombination (loopChainAlgebra Circle 1 R)
          (loopCellComparison H R Circle.expLoop.toMooreLoop) u' +
        cubicalChainModuleDifferential (MoorePathFrom Circle 1) H R v = w :=
  (forall_exists_loopCellComparison_iff_forall_exists_loopCellCocycle _).2
    (fun _ hu hε ↦ exists_loopCellCocycle_expLoop_differential_eq_of_loopCellAugmentation_eq_zero
      hu hε) u w hu huw

end Circle

end TauCeti
